              "text": "## Task Splitting - clearAllTasks Mode\n\n## Splitting Strategy\n\n1. **Functional Decomposition** - Independent testable sub-functions with clear inputs and outputs\n2. **Technical Layer Decomposition** - Separate tasks along architectural layers, ensuring clear interfaces\n3. **Development Stage Decomposition** - Core functionality first, optimization features later\n4. **Risk-based Decomposition** - Isolate high-risk parts, reduce overall risk\n\n## Task Quality Review\n\n1. **Task Atomicity** - Each task is small and specific enough to be completed independently\n2. **Dependencies** - Task dependencies form a directed acyclic graph, avoiding circular dependencies\n3. **Description Completeness** - Each task description is clear and accurate, including necessary context\n\n## Task List\n\n### Task 1: Design Real-Time Data Ingestion Pipeline\n\n**ID:** `66e5cd7d-bafe-4c1c-88da-b9988e99cb4b`\n**Description:** Set up a system to ingest real-time transportation data from multiple sources (e.g., GPS, traffic sensors, public transit APIs) using REST and WebSocket protocols with low-latency streaming.\n\n**Notes:** Ensure data arrives within sub-second latency and includes metadata like source, timestamp, and location.\n\n**Implementation Guide:** Use Apache Kafka or MQTT for message streaming. Implement data validation and schema enforcement at ...\n\n**Verification Criteria:** Verify data ingestion latency is under 100ms and all data points are correctly timestamped and sourc...\n\n**Dependencies:** \n\n### Task 2: Preprocess and Clean Real-Time Data\n\n**ID:** `01ece73a-6acb-48ff-ba94-7754eb368326`\n**Description:** Clean and normalize incoming transportation data to remove noise, handle missing values, and filter outliers before route optimization.\n\n**Notes:** Maintain data integrity and ensure preprocessing does not introduce bias or distort real-time conditions.\n\n**Implementation Guide:** Apply data cleaning rules (e.g., interpolate miss