\n\n**Notes:** Ensure the UI is intuitive and provides clear visual feedback on route changes.\n\n**Implementation Guide:** Use a modern UI framework (e.g., React or Vue) to build a responsive interface. Include features lik...\n\n**Verification Criteria:** Verify that the UI displays live route updates, traffic conditions, and alternative options clearly ...\n\n**Dependencies:** \"Build Real-Time Feedback System\" (`43756e31-7e20-497b-95c1-f2ea9567329a`)\n\n### Task 6: Integrate Performance Monitoring and Logging\n\n**ID:** `ef930470-1124-41f5-9d49-812fa3b3ea9c`\n**Description:** Add logging and monitoring to track response times, accuracy, and system stability of the route optimization system.\n\n**Notes:** Ensure logs are structured and include timestamps, source, and error codes.\n\n**Implementation Guide:** Implement logging for key events (e.g., data ingestion, route computation, UI updates). Use metrics ...\n\n**Verification Criteria:** Verify that logs capture all key events and metrics are available for real-time monitoring.\n\n**Dependencies:** \"Build Real-Time Feedback System\" (`43756e31-7e20-497b-95c1-f2ea9567329a`)\n\n\n## Dependency Management\n\n- Dependencies can be set using task names or task IDs\n- Minimize the number of dependencies, only set direct prerequisite tasks\n- Avoid circular dependencies, ensure the task graph is directed and acyclic\n- Balance the critical path, optimize possibilities for parallel execution\n\n## Decision Points\n\n- If task splitting is found unreasonable: call \"split_tasks\" again to adjust\n- If task splitting is confirmed to be sound: generate execution plan, determine priorities\n\n**Severe Warning** Each time you call split_tasks, the parameters you pass cannot exceed 5000 characters. If it exceeds 5000 characters, please call the tool multiple times to complete\n\n**If there are remaining tasks, please continue to call \"split_tasks\"**\n",
